        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 39.08,
        "asr_text": "The problem was not that humans made the calls. The problem was how users were told who was speaking. People who asked MUse to make a call might think AI was doing it, but sometimes a human was speaking instead. If this was not explained clearly, users could not know if it was AI or a person. They enjoyed the ease of AI, but they did not know that a human was on the other end. This was happening behind the scenes. Also, a call might need user information to continue. That information might then be shared by mistake with contract workers at a call center. Meta employees raised this inside the company as a privacy concern.",
